# Validation: default is **skip** (maintainer policy)

**The maintainer does not want agents running `npm run check`, `npm run test:quick`, or `npm run verify` after routine coding.** They have asked repeatedly. Treat “skip validation” as the default for every session.

## Do **not** run `npm run check` (unless a bullet below says otherwise)

- **Any routine game/UI work**: small edits, one-file fixes, conditionals, styling, copy, new components, quest tweaks, village/tavern layout, etc.
- Changes are **docs/markdown only**, **Cursor rules**, **image/assets**, or copy-only with no build tooling.
- The user’s request is **read-only** (explain, review, plan) with **no file edits**.
- You already ran check **successfully in this session** on the same working tree and nothing relevant changed since.
- **When in doubt: skip.** Do not “be helpful” by running check.

## Run `npm run check` **only** when

1. The user **explicitly asks** (e.g. “run check”, “verify”, “make sure CI passes”), **or**
2. The change is **serious / high-risk**, for example:
   - build tooling, `package.json` deps/scripts, `tsconfig`, eslint/vite config
   - broad refactors across many files or shared types/APIs
   - release-critical or CI-breaking risk the user called out
   - you genuinely cannot ship without typecheck (e.g. complex generic/types work) **and** the user would care — still prefer asking first if unsure

## Escalation (even rarer)

- **`npm run test:quick`**: only if the user asks **or** you changed behavior under existing tests and they asked for test confidence.
- **`npm run verify`**: only if the user explicitly asks, or release/tooling/high-risk per above.

## Anti-patterns (do not do these)

- Running check **after every TS touch** or “to finish the task”.
- Running check **twice** without new edits.
- Running check after **only** bumping `package.json` version.
- Backgrounding check “because the rules said to” on a trivial diff.

**Summary:** Skip check unless the user asked or the change is seriously risky. The maintainer will run checks locally when they want them.
